PARSFILE
#FullDataName Models: Simulink`Semi-Active Suspension`Suspension and Suspension Controls
#RunMdlFile Extensions\Simulink\SemiActive_Susp_CS9.mdl
#RingCtrl1 2
OPT_INT_METHOD 2
#CheckBox0 0    
*USE_ALT_DIR 0
#CheckBox1 0    
*USE_DIFF_SOLVERS 0
#CheckBox2 1    
OPT_IO_UPDATE 1
#CheckBox3 1    

*TSTEP 0.001
*FREQ_MODEL 1000
*TSTEP_OUT 0.025
*FREQ_OUT 40
tstep 0.001
iprint 25
PARSFILE IO_Channels\I_Channels\Import_a701d810-39be-458f-b86d-ef2e1d9e0cf7.par
#BlueLink0 I/O Channels: Import`Semi-Active Suspension` Steering and Susp. Imports` , Import`Import_a701d810-39be-458f-b86d-ef2e1d9e0cf7

PARSFILE IO_Channels\O_Channels\Export_0d6d31d9-7ed5-48a2-b18b-fecaef530d8c.par
#BlueLink1 I/O Channels: Export`Semi-Active Suspension` Steering and Susp. Exports` , Export`Export_0d6d31d9-7ed5-48a2-b18b-fecaef530d8c

LIVE_SERVER_UPDATE_FREQ_MAX 60

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset links to a Simulink model of a Semi-Active suspension system.
#
#The Simulink model is set to use "variable step" numerical integration, which means it will inherit the time step from CarSim.
#
#In this case, the time step is set at 0.001, the method is AM-2, and the option is checked to communicate with Simulink at an interval of 1/2 the time step (i.e., 0.0005 sec).
#
#The Import and Export Channels links specify variables sent to (exported) and returned from (imported) the Simulink model. In this case, the shock absorber forces from CarSim are replaced with forces imported from Simulink.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Models: Simulink; { Suspension and Suspension Controls } Semi-Active Suspension
#Library : Models: Simulink
#DataSet : Semi-Active Suspension
#Category: Suspension and Suspension Controls
#FileID  : Simlink_ec90090a-571c-4a0f-98ac-1d14d3f80d97
#Product : CarSim 2017.1
#VehCode 

